mment":""},{"DocComment":" * For structs whose last field is a DST, metadata is the metadata for the last field"},{"DocComment":" * For the `str` type, metadata is the length in bytes as `usize`"},{"DocComment":" * For slice types like `[T]`, metadata is the length in items as `usize`"},{"DocComment":" * For trait objects like `dyn SomeTrait`, metadata is [`DynMetadata<Self>`][DynMetadata]"},{"DocComment":"   (e.g. `DynMetadata<dyn SomeTrait>`)"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" In the future, the Rust language may gain new kinds of types"},{"DocComment":" that have different pointer metadata."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [dst]: https://doc.rust-lang.org/nomicon/exotic-sizes.html#dynamically-sized-types-dsts"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # The `Pointee` trait"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The point of this trait is its `Metadata` associated type,"},{"DocComment":" which is `()` or `usize` or `DynMetadata<_>` as described above."},{"DocComment":" It is automatically implemented for every type."},{"DocComment":" It can be assumed to be implemented in a generic context, even without a corresponding bound."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Usage"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Raw pointers can be decomposed into the data pointer and metadata components"},{"DocComment":" with their [`to_raw_parts`] method."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Alternatively, metadata alone can be extracted with the [`metadata`] function."},{"DocComment":" A reference can be passed to [`metadata`] and implicitly coerced."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" A (possibly-wide) pointer can be put back together from its data pointer and metadata"},{"DocComment":" with [`from_raw_parts`] or [`from_raw_parts_mut`]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`to_raw_parts`]: *const::to_raw_parts"}],"inline":null,"rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":"pointee_trait"},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"